       headers (CaseInsensitiveDict): A case-insensitive dictionary\n   170→            containing all the headers in the response, except for\n   171→            cookies, which may be accessed via the `cookies`\n   172→            attribute.\n   173→\n   174→            Note:\n   175→\n   176→                Multiple instances of a header in the response are\n   177→                currently not supported; it is unspecified which value\n   178→                will \"win\" and be represented in `headers`.\n   179→\n   180→        cookies (dict): A dictionary of\n   181→            :py:class:`falcon.testing.Cookie` values parsed from the\n   182→            response, by name.\n   183→\n   184→            The cookies dictionary can be used directly in subsequent requests::\n   185→\n   186→                client = testing.TestClient(app)\n   187→                response_one = client.simulate_get('/')\n   188→                response_two = client.simulate_post('/', cookies=response_one.cookies)\n   189→\n   190→        encoding (str): Text encoding of the response body, or ``None``\n   191→            if the encoding can not be determined.\n   192→    \"\"\"\n   193→\n   194→    def __init__(self, status, headers):\n   195→        self._status = status\n   196→        self._status_code = int(status[:3])\n   197→        self._headers = CaseInsensitiveDict(headers)\n   198→\n   199→        cookies = http_cookies.SimpleCookie()\n   200→        for name, value in headers:\n   201→            if name.lower() == 'set-cookie':\n   202→                cookies.load(value)\n   203→\n   204→        self._cookies = dict(\n   205→            (morsel.key, Cookie(morsel)) for morsel in cookies.values()\n   206→        )\n   207→\n   208→        self._encoding = helpers.get_encoding_from_headers(self._headers)\n   209→\n   210→    @property\n   211→    def status(self) -> str:\n   212→        return self._status\n   213→\n   214→    @property\n   215→    def status_code(self) -> int:\n   216→        return self._status_code\n   217→\n   218→    @property\n   219→    def headers(self) -> CaseInsensitiveDict:\n   220→        # NOTE(kgriffs): It would probably be better to annotate this with\n   221→        #   a generic Mapping[str, str] type, but currently there is an\n   222→        #   incompatibility with Cython that prevents us from modifying\n   223→        #   CaseInsensitiveDict to inherit from a generic MutableMapping\n   224→        #   type. This might be resolved in the future by moving\n   225→        #   the CaseInsensitiveDict implementation to the falcon.testing\n   226→        #   module so that it is no longer cythonized.\n   227→        return self._headers\n   228→\n   229→    @property\n   230→    def cookies(self) -> Dict[str, Cookie]:\n   231→        return self._cookies\n   232→\n   233→    @property\n   234→    def encoding(self) -> str:\n   235→        return self._encoding\n   236→\n   237→\n   238→class ResultBodyStream:\n   239→    \"\"\"Simple forward-only reader for a streamed test result body.\n   240→\n   241→    Args:\n   242→        chunks (list): Reference to a list of body chunks that may\n   243→            continue to be appended to as more body events are\n   244→            collected.\n   245→    \"\"\"\n   246→\n   247→    def __init__(self, chunks: Sequence[bytes]):\n   248→        self._chunks = chunks\n   249→        self._chunk_pos = 0\n   250→\n   251→    async def read(self) -> bytes:\n   252→        \"\"\"Read any data that has been collected since the last call.\n   253→\n   254→        Returns:\n   255→            bytes: data that has been collected since the last call,\n   256→            or an empty byte string if no additional data is available.\n   257→        \"\"\"\n   258→\n   259→        # NOTE(kgriffs): Yield to other tasks to give them a chance to\n   260→        #   send us more body chunks if any are available.\n   261→        #\n   262→        #   https://bugs.python.org/issue34476\n   263→        #\n   264→        await asyncio.sleep(0)\n   265→\n   266→        if self._chunk_pos >= len(self._chunks):\n   267→            return b''\n   268→\n   269→        data = b''.join(self._chunks[self._chunk_pos :])\n   270→        self._chunk_pos = len(self._chunks)\n   271→\n   272→        return data\n   273→\n   274→\n   275→class Result(_ResultBase):\n   276→    \"\"\"Encapsulates the result of a simulated request.\n   277→\n   278→    Args:\n   279→        iterable (iterable): An iterable that yields zero or more\n   280→            bytestrings, per PEP-3333\n   281→        status (str): An HTTP status string, including status code and\n   282→            reason string\n   283→        headers (list): A list of (header_name, header_value) tuples,\n   284→            per PEP-3333\n   285→\n   286→    Attributes:\n   287→        status (str): HTTP status string given in the response\n   288→        status_code (int): The code portion of the HTTP status string\n   289→        headers (CaseInsensitiveDict): A case-insensitive dictionary\n   290→            containing all the headers in the response, except for\n   291→            cookies, which may be accessed via the `cookies`\n   292→            attribute.\n   293→\n   294→            Note:\n   295→\n   296→                Multiple instances of a header in the response are\n   297→                currently not supported; it is unspecified which value\n   298→                will \"win\" and be represented in `headers`.\n   299→\n   300→        cookies (dict): A dictionary of\n   301→            :py:class:`falcon.testing.Cookie` values parsed from the\n   302→            response, by name.\n   303→        encoding (str): Text encoding of the response body, or ``None``\n   304→            if the encoding can not be determined.\n   305→        content (bytes): Raw response body, or ``bytes`` if the\n   306→            response body was empty.\n   307→        text (str): Decoded response body of type ``str``.\n   308→            If the content type does not specify an encoding, UTF-8 is\n   309→            assumed.\n   310→        json (JSON serializable): Deserialized JSON body. Will be ``None`` if\n   311→            the body has no content to deserialize. Otherwise, raises an error\n   312→            if the response is not valid JSON.\n   313→    \"\"\"\n   314→\n   315→    def __init__(self, iterable, status, headers):\n   316→        super().__init__(status, headers)\n   317→\n   318→        self._text = None\n   319→        self._content = b''.join(iterable)\n   320→\n   321→    @property\n   322→    def content(self) -> bytes:\n   323→        return self._content\n   324→\n   325→    @property\n   326→    def text(self) -> str:\n   327→        if self._text is None:\n   328→            if not self.content:\n   329→                self._text = ''\n   330→            else:\n   331→                if self.encoding is None:\n   332→                    encoding = 'UTF-8'\n   333→                else:\n   334→                    encoding = self.encoding\n   335→\n   336→                self._text = self.content.decode(encoding)\n   337→\n   338→        return self._text\n   339→\n   340→    @property\n   341→    def json(self) -> Optional[Union[dict, list, str, int, float, bool]]:\n   342→        if not self.text:\n   343→            return None\n   344→\n   345→        return json_module.loads(self.text)\n   346→\n   347→    def __repr__(self):\n   348→        content_type = self.headers.get('Content-Type', '')\n   349→\n   350→        if len(self.content) > 40:\n   351→            content = self.content[:20] + b'...' + self.content[-20:]\n   352→        else:\n   353→            content = self.content\n   354→\n   355→        args = [self.status, content_type, str(content)]\n   356→\n   357→        repr_result = ' '.join(filter(None, args))\n   358→        return 'Result<{}>'.format(repr_result)\n   359→\n   360→\n   361→class StreamedResult(_ResultBase):\n   362→    \"\"\"Encapsulates the streamed result of an ASGI request.\n   363→\n   364→    Args:\n   365→        body_chunks (list): A list of body chunks. This list may be\n   366→            appended to after a result object has been instantiated.\n   367→        status (str): An HTTP status string, including status code and\n   368→            reason string\n   369→        headers (list): A list of (header_name, header_value) tuples,\n   370→            per PEP-3333\n   371→        task (asyncio.Task): The scheduled simulated request which may or\n   372→            may not have already finished. :meth:`~.finalize`\n   373→            will await the task before returning.\n   374→        req_event_emitter (~falcon.testing.ASGIRequestEventEmitter): A reference\n   375→            to the event emitter used to simulate events sent to the ASGI\n   376→            application via its receive() method.\n   377→            :meth:`~.finalize` will cause the event emitter to\n   378→            simulate an ``'http.disconnect'`` event before returning.\n   379→\n   380→    Attributes:\n   381→        status (str): HTTP status string given in the response\n   382→        status_code (int): The code portion of the HTTP status string\n   383→        headers (CaseInsensitiveDict): A case-insensitive dictionary\n   384→            containing all the headers in the response, except for\n   385→            cookies, which may be accessed via the `cookies`\n   386→            attribute.\n   387→\n   388→            Note:\n   389→\n   390→                Multiple instances of a header in the response are\n   391→                currently not supported; it is unspecified which value\n   392→                will \"win\" and be represented in `headers`.\n   393→\n   394→        cookies (dict): A dictionary of\n   395→            :py:class:`falcon.testing.Cookie` values parsed from the\n   396→            response, by name.\n   397→        encoding (str): Text encoding of the response body, or