ion__}'\n  1863→\n  1864→        body (str): The body of the request (default ''). The value will be\n  1865→            encoded as UTF-8 in the WSGI environ. Alternatively, a byte string\n  1866→            may be passed, in which case it will be used as-is.\n  1867→        json(JSON serializable): A JSON document to serialize as the\n  1868→            body of the request (default: ``None``). If specified,\n  1869→            overrides `body` and sets the Content-Type header to\n  1870→            ``'application/json'``, overriding any value specified by either\n  1871→            the `content_type` or `headers` arguments.\n  1872→        host(str): A string to use for the hostname part of the fully\n  1873→            qualified request URL (default: 'falconframework.org')\n  1874→        remote_addr (str): A string to use as the remote IP address for the\n  1875→            request (default: '127.0.0.1'). For WSGI, this corresponds to\n  1876→            the 'REMOTE_ADDR' environ variable. For ASGI, this corresponds\n  1877→            to the IP address used for the 'client' field in the connection\n  1878→            scope.\n  1879→        http_version (str): The HTTP version to simulate. Must be either\n  1880→            '2', '2.0', 1.1', '1.0', or '1' (default '1.1'). If set to '1.0',\n  1881→            the Host header will not be added to the scope.\n  1882→        wsgierrors (io): The stream to use as *wsgierrors* in the WSGI\n  1883→            environ (default ``sys.stderr``)\n  1884→        asgi_chunk_size (int): The maximum number of bytes that will be\n  1885→            sent to the ASGI app in a single ``'http.request'`` event (default\n  1886→            4096).\n  1887→        asgi_disconnect_ttl (int): The maximum number of seconds to wait\n  1888→            since the request was initiated, before emitting an\n  1889→            ``'http.disconnect'`` event when the app calls the\n  1890→            receive() function (default 300). Set to ``0`` to